---
description: graphify knowledge graph context
alwaysApply: true
---

This project has a graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`.

**Prefer graphify for codebase exploration** when the `graphify` CLI is on `PATH`
(typically via `~/.local/bin` after `uv tool install graphifyy`) and
`graphify-out/graph.json` exists. Before broad Read/Grep/Glob exploration, run:
- `graphify query "<question>"` — scoped subgraph for architecture questions
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — dependency path between two symbols
- `graphify explain "<concept>"` — neighbors of a concept

If `graphify` is missing from `PATH`, or `graphify-out/graph.json` is absent, fall
back to normal Read/Grep/Glob — do not block on graphify.

Include this guidance in subagent prompts that explore code. Prefer graphify over
grep for cross-file dependency questions when it is available.

- If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, navigate it instead of reading raw files
- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for broad architecture review when
  query/path/explain do not surface enough context
- After modifying code files, run `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost),
  then **stage and commit the `graphify-out/` changes with the same change set**
  (or a follow-up commit on the same branch). The graph is tracked in git;
  leaving it dirty after an env-style refresh is incorrect. Do not rely on
  Cursor Cloud environment install to regenerate it.
